{
 "chapter": 37,
 "title": "Two different kinds of fear",
 "duration": 123.06666666666626,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 4.866666666666667,
   "end": 15.787074829931973,
   "text": "Replay the bad news principle from chapter nine. When you can wait, it is mainly the bad possible outcomes that decide whether you build now.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 16.999999999999996,
   "end": 21.914195011337867,
   "text": "So the question to ask is: what does this policy actually compress?",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 24.26666666666666,
   "end": 28.219909297052148,
   "text": "the price of risk. Extra return, for the worry.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 32.533333333333346,
   "end": 39.44911564625852,
   "text": "In financial markets, quantitative easing pushes that price down. Squeeze the spring.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.33333333333358,
   "end": 44.858775510204325,
   "text": "Will there still be customers in three years?",
   "voice": "c"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.26666666666695,
   "end": 48.765986394558105,
   "text": "Will the euro survive, or will countries start leaving it?",
   "voice": "c"
  },
  {
   "start": 49.20000000000032,
   "end": 51.93419501133819,
   "text": "Will this whole industry still exist?",
   "voice": "c"
  },
  {
   "start": 53.133333333333695,
   "end": 62.14045351473959,
   "text": "Those are different worries entirely. A central bank buying government bonds reaches them only indirectly, if at all.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 64.93333333333372,
   "end": 69.08394557823168,
   "text": "He cannot say the policy fails to touch that fear.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 69.53333333333369,
   "end": 74.15995464852644,
   "text": "Higher share and property prices do make some owners spend more.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 74.60000000000032,
   "end": 81.00294784580531,
   "text": "And one company's customers are other people's spending. So the fear is thinned a little.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 81.40000000000029,
   "end": 88.67569160997762,
   "text": "And buying government bonds is obviously aimed at doubts about governments in the first place.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 90.40000000000022,
   "end": 95.98857142857165,
   "text": "So the honest version of his claim is about how directly, not about whether.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.20000000000009,
   "end": 108.04897959183683,
   "text": "What a central bank reaches directly is the price at which risk trades. What it reaches at one or two removes is the doubt itself.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 110.33333333333327,
   "end": 112.21999999999994,
   "text": "bad news principle",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 112.3333333333332,
   "end": 114.93981859410418,
   "text": "QE squeezes the price of risk",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 115.06666666666646,
   "end": 118.18399092970502,
   "text": "a different fear: will there be customers?",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 118.33333333333307,
   "end": 120.66988662131493,
   "text": "how DIRECTLY \u2014 not whether",
   "voice": "n"
  }
 ],
